   "title": "Thirteen test points on the silkscreen, nine jumpers in the parts list",
   "text": "The board is silkscreened TP1 to TP13 and the sheet 1 legend names all thirteen. Table 6-24 lists JUMPER,WIRE,NONINSUL for TP1-5, TP8, TP10, TP12 and TP13 only — nine, and the Tot Qty column agrees. So TP6 (RESETL), TP7 (+12VUR), TP9 (-12VUR) and TP11 (+5VUR) are labelled pads with no wire loop fitted. They are still real probe targets and are placed and carried here, marked notInParts; what they take is a probe tip rather than a clip lead. Both sources are right about their own subject, so neither has been 'corrected'.",
