   "title": "What the two parts lists disagree about",
   "text": "Thirteen rows differ between the 1996 Series II list (Table 6-24) and the Rev 9 list, and every one of them is a real revision difference rather than a scanning artefact. Two change the part: CR25–CR28 are DIODE,SI,50 PIV,3.0 AMP / MR850 in Rev 9 — which is what the schematic prints — and DIODE,SI,150 PIV,5.0 AMP in 1996; H2 changes from a stainless to a steel screw; M1/M2 and VR5 (1N753A in Rev 9) change stock number and supplier. The other nine are the carbon-film resistors R1, R2, R3/R12, R4, R6, R7, R8, R9/R11 and R10, whose descriptions are identical in both revisions but whose Fluke stock numbers are not — a re-sourcing, not a change of part. R5 and R13 kept their numbers. The Rev 9 entry is carried as 'as built' on each affected part, since Rev 9 is the revision the drawing and the photographed board match.",
